      "date_last_updated": "2026-10-07T13:42:42.160919+00:00",
      "description": "New Snapd release 2.78 is required for jammy, noble, resolute, stonking.\n\nSnapd 2.78 is the latest upstream release. It follows the previous Ubuntu release snapd 2.77.1\n\nThe Snapd package deviates from the standard SRU process. The following special SRU process was followed: https://github.com/ubuntu/ubuntu-project-docs/pull/542\n\nRelease preparation: https://github.com/canonical/snapd/pull/17585\nRelease preparation test results: https://github.com/canonical/snapd/actions/runs/33890426609\nFailure analysis: https://github.com/canonical/snapd/pull/17585#issuecomment-5568882382\n\nRelease notes: https://github.com/canonical/snapd/pull/17585/changes#diff-51920e95310ebfbc1ae31709f3b95f89afffbf4f1a6e38e8b2b406e2fb6197ea\n\nPlease refer to snapd release notes documentation (https://github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/master/RELEASE.md) for details on how this is assembled.\n\nLaunchpad bugs addressed: https://launchpad.net/snapd/+milestone/2.78\n\nContent overview:\n\npackaging:\n- introduce a downstream version suffix to manipulate rather than the full version\n- workaround dh_golang, drop prepare-debian-build-tree\n\nother:\n- FDE reprovisioning\n- confdb and remote device management\n- graduating quota-groups features\n- enabling by default refresh-app-awareness-ux\n- improve disk space checks and add disk-reservation.size option\n- snap removal improvements\n- component improvements\n- security logging\n- merge more tools into multi-entry binary\n- fix an issue with little kernel bootloader\n- fix various hybrid remodeling issues\n- improve robustness of seed refresh prerequisites\n- various interface fixes and improvements and added the new ubuntu-drivers-observe interface\n\nSource packages on ppa:snappy-dev/image for upload to -proposed:\n\nstonking https://launchpad.net/~snappy-dev/+archive/ubuntu/image/+sourcepub/18721810/+listing-archive-extra\n\nresolute https://launchpad.net/~snappy-dev/+archive/ubuntu/image/+sourcepub/18721809/+listing-archive-extra\n\nnoble https://launchpad.net/~snappy-dev/+archive/ubuntu/image/+sourcepub/18721808/+listing-archive-extra\n\njammy https://launchpad.net/~snappy-dev/+archive/ubuntu/image/+sourcepub/18721807/+listing-archive-extra\n\nValidation already completed:\n\n- Release preparation test results: https://github.com/canonical/snapd/actions/runs/33890426609\n\nVerification required:\n\n- QA Beta validation https://warthogs.atlassian.net/browse/SNAPDENG-37484\n- Certification validation: https://test-observer.canonical.com/#/snaps/412660 (need VPN)\n- Verify LP bugs for jammy, noble, resolute, stonking\n- Perform release upgrades from jammy to stonking",
      "description_sha": "0ca3e7ac93f7538721c8a0d88a8abffbf0598133ff25ce3cda1ccbcb6d206368",
